  data: {
    LLM: "1. Turning: Players take turns (clockwise) drawing one card from either the stock or discard pile, then discarding one card.\n2. Duration: The game lasts exactly SIX rounds. After the dealer's sixth turn, the play ends.\n3. Showdown: Players divide their 7 cards into a 4ndcard hand and a 3ndcard hand. They show the 4ndcard hands first to determine the winner, then the 3ndcard hands.",
    Player: "1. Turning: Players take turns (clockwise) drawing one card from either the stock or discard pile, then discarding one card.\n2. Duration: The game lasts exactly SIX rounds. After the dealer's sixth turn, the play ends.\n3. Showdown: Players divide their 7 cards into a 4ndcard hand and a 3ndcard hand. They show the 4ndcard hands first to determine the winner, then the 3ndcard hands.",
    objective: "Win the pot by having the highest-ranking 4ndcard 'Going Down' hand and 3ndcard 'Coming Back' hand.",
    gameplay: "1. Turning: Players take turns (clockwise) drawing one card from either the stock or discard pile, then discarding one card.\n2. Duration: The game lasts exactly SIX rounds. After the dealer's sixth turn, the play ends.\n3. Showdown: Players divide their 7 cards into a 4ndcard hand and a 3ndcard hand. They show the 4ndcard hands first to determine the winner, then the 3ndcard hands.",
    keyRules: [
      'Aces are always low (A-2-3-4 is valid, J-Q-KndA is NOT).',
      'Hand Ties: If two players tie for the best hand, they cut cards from the deck; the higher cut wins.',
      "The pot is often split between the winner of the 'Going Down' hand and the 'Coming Back' hand.",
